      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1hgdkhs'
    '|a||And the payoff? A better-informed vote changes the outcome only if yours is the vote that breaks a tie.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:s7x920'
    '|b||Andrew Gelman, Nate Silver and Aaron Edlin worked out those odds for the 2008 US presidential election: on average, one in sixty million.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:dxr3as'
    '|a||Now say the better result is worth five thousand dollars to you, a lot. Multiply it by one in sixty million.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1rpme1w'
    '|b||Less than a hundredth of a cent. Against two hundred dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ykeo7u'
    '|a||That''s rational ignorance, Anthony Downs''s idea from 1957: when your vote almost never decides, studying for it doesn''t pay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ajhnxn'
    '|b||Still under two cents.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Even in the closest states, about one in ten million, a million-dollar stake buys ten cents.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:pa7rof'
    '|b||Want to see the sum?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:w7gwh1'
    '|b||Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:dqz85n'
    '|a||The expected benefit is the chance your vote decides, p, times what the outcome is worth to you, B.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Five thousand dollars over sixty million is about eight thousandths of a cent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15ggx42'
    '|a||Learning pays only if p times B beats the cost, two hundred dollars. It never comes close.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1d69b0t'
    '|a||So the voter''s ignorance isn''t a lapse. It''s the right answer to her sum, and everyone in politics can count on it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1h138is'
    '|a||Ignorance is the voter''s best deal, and a politician can count on it. Watch what that does in Harbourtown.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Say Mia''s bakery asks the harbour council for a one-dollar fee on every loaf shipped in from the mainland.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1mhotd3'
    '|a||With the cheaper mainland bread held back, Mia can charge more. Illustrative numbers: she gains thirty thousand dollars a year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1w47ljr'
    '|b||And each of the town''s six thousand people pays about six dollars a year more for bread. On this chart, a sliver.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:76bbas'
    '|b||So who turns up at the council meeting?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1tba5wh'
    '|a||Mia and her bakers. Thirty thousand dollars is worth an evening; six dollars isn''t worth reading the agenda.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1afpudc'
    '|b||But the council''s clerk can multiply. Six thousand people times six dollars is thirty-six thousand. The town loses more than Mia gains.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ro9c07'
    '|b||Then surely the council says no. The numbers are right there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1n35ur7'
    '|a||How does a councillor who wants to be re-elected vote on the fee?':
      mp3: 
